%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% These are health notes, not a Coach training-results feature. Route has authenticate / validate, no invented Coach authorization restriction.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Member
    participant UI as API client
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as enrollmentsController
    participant S as enrollmentsService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Edit own enrollment health notes and optionally save to profile
    UI->>API: PATCH /api/v1/enrollments/:id/health-notes
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: updateEnrollmentHealthNotes(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: updateEnrollmentHealthNotes(id, userId, role, healthNotes, saveToProfile)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Read enrollment with member ownership and schedule
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Member must own this enrollment, normalize whitespace-only notes to null
        alt enrollment missing or another Member owns it
            S-->>C: 404 / 403
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Transaction updates enrollment.healthNotes and optional nonempty MemberProfile.healthNotes
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S-->>C: Updated enrollment health notes
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error
%% UI_SCOPE: Backend/API implemented. Current application UI route is not verified as reachable.

